Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement per-key stateful streaming logic, rolling window calculations, and safe downstream signaling with offset semantics. It also probes handling of out-of-order arrivals and ensuring at-least-once delivery by committing only after alert emission succeeds.

Key Concepts
- Per-key state management
- Rolling window calculations (60s)
- Threshold-based anomaly detection
- Idempotent downstream writes and offset commits
- Canary test design for spike vs. normal data

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for onMessage
class RuleEngine {
  constructor(windowMs=60000) {
    this.windowMs = windowMs;
    this.state = new Map(); // sensorId -> [{ts,value}, ...], plus sum/count
  }
  onMessage(event){
    const {sensorId, ts, value} = event;
    const bucket = this.state.get(sensorId) || {q:[], sum:0, count:0};
    // prune old
    while (bucket.q.length && bucket.q[0].ts <= ts - this.windowMs) {
      const old = bucket.q.shift(); bucket.sum -= old.value; bucket.count--;
    }
    bucket.q.push({ts,value}); bucket.sum += value; bucket.count++;
    const avg = bucket.count ? bucket.sum / bucket.count : value;
    if (value > 1.2 * avg) { this.emitAlert(sensorId, ts, value, avg); }
    this.state.set(sensorId, bucket);
  }
  rollingAvgFor(sensorId){ const bucket = this.state.get(sensorId); return bucket?.count ? bucket.sum / bucket.count : null; }
  emitAlert(sensorId, ts, value, avg){ // write to threshold_alerts sink
    // sink.write({sensorId, ts, value, avg});
  }
  commitOffsets(){ /* commit after sink write */ }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Cross-region locality is real; this tests ordering, fault tolerance, and cross-region controls with per-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant locality constraints
- Vector clocks for per-tenant ordering
- Commit barriers and selective replication
- Idempotent apply and deduplication

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo per-tenant apply with idempotence
function applyEvent(tenantId, event, state) {
  const last = state[tenantId]?.seq ?? 0;
  if (event.seq <= last) return state;
  state[tenantId] = { seq: event.seq, data: event.data };
  return state;
}
```

