## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time handling of dynamic policies, data privacy, and end-to-end guarantees in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic per-tenant policy loading from a KCNA topic
- Real-time cache updates with atomic policy changes
- Data redaction strategies (none, partial, full)
- Idempotent sinks and at-least-once guarantees
- Testing under policy updates and message reordering

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(customer, level) {
  if (level === 'full') return { name: null, email: null, card: null };
  if (level === 'partial') {
    const maskedCard = customer.card.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
    const maskedEmail = customer.email.replace(/([^@]{1,2})[^@]*(@.*)/, (m, p1, p2) => p1[0] + '**' + p2);
    return { ...customer, card: maskedCard, email: maskedEmail };
  }
  return customer;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical KCNA routing pattern: per-message fan-out with per-destination ordering and safe offset commits.

## Key Concepts
- Per-destination routing and ordering
- Offset management: commit after downstream ack
- Outbox pattern and idempotent sinks
- Retries and backoff
- Canary testing for correctness

## Code Example
```javascript
class RouteFanoutProcessor {
  onMessage(msg) {
    const dest = msg.headers.dest;
    const target = `sink-${dest}`;
    return publish(target, msg.payload).then(() => ack(msg.offset));
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to many destinations and hot keys?
- How would you guarantee approximate exactly-once with external sinks?
- How would you instrument latency and ordering per destination?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests stateful cross-topic streaming, per-key windowing, offset management, and recovery semantics within KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Stateful cross-topic join for userId
- Per-topic offset preservation and replay safety
- 15-second tumbling window with watermark handling
- State snapshotting to a compacted 'kcna_state' topic
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once emission guarantees and dedup

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: join processor sketch
class JoinProcessor {
  constructor() {
    this.profileCache = new Map();
    this.window = new TumblingWindow(15); // in seconds
  }
  onClick(click) {
    const pid = this.profileCache.get(click.userId);
    if (pid) emitEnriched({ ...click, profileVersion: pid.version });
    // else stash or wait for profile
  }
  onProfile(profile) {
    this.profileCache.set(profile.userId, profile);
  }
  onWindowEmit(windowId) {
    // snapshot state to kcna_state and commit
  }
}
```
